  "generated_text": "Let $q(x) = p(x) - \\frac{1}{x^2}.$  Then $q(x)$ is a cubic polynomial, and $q(1) = q(2) = q(3) = q(4) = 0.$  Therefore, $q(x) = (x - 1)(x - 2)(x - 3)(x - 4) r(x)$ for some polynomial $r(x).$  Hence,\n\\[p(x) = \\frac{1}{x^2} + (x - 1)(x - 2)(x - 3)(x - 4) r(x).\\]In particular,\n\\[p(5) = \\frac{1}{5^2} + (4)(3)(2)(1) r(5) = \\frac{1}{25} + 24 r(5).\\]Since $r(5)$ can be any real number, the smallest possible value of $p(5)$ is $\\frac{1}{25}.$  Therefore, $p(5) = \\boxed{\\frac{1}{25}}.$The answer is: \\boxed{\\frac{1}{25}}",
